WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Put an electrical heater
into a metal block,

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.900
and time how fast its temperature rises.

3
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.780
From your readings, you work out the
energy each kilogram needs per degree.

4
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.380
You get 960 joules.

5
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.980
The data book says about 900.

6
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.630
Your value is too high.

7
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.120
Some energy always leaks away.

8
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.390
So how can you measure what
the material really needs?

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.140
In this mission, you'll
build the heater circuit,

10
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.200
and record the temperature
every 30 seconds.

11
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:34.780
Then you'll melt ice and boil water, to
measure the energy needed to change state.

12
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:39.110
Your mission: find out how to
measure the energy a material needs,

13
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.910
even when some leaks away.
